### Bot API 10.4 (November 9, 2026)

#### Widgets

- Added `sendWidget`, `sendSharedWidget`, `answerWidgetQuery`, `editMessageWidgetData`, and `editSharedWidgetData`.
- Added `Widget` and `widget` on `Message` and `ExternalReplyInfo`.
- Added `WidgetQuery`/`SharedWidgetQuery` and the `widget_query`/`shared_widget_query` update types, plus `WidgetQueryType` (`WidgetQueryTypeData`, `WidgetQueryTypeSignData`, `WidgetQueryTypeSentTransaction`) and `WidgetQueryWallet`.
- Added `InputWidgetMessageContent` and `InputSharedWidgetMessageContent`.
- `ctx.chat`/`ctx.from` resolve for widget queries (`shared_widget_query` has no chat).

```ts
await bot.api.sendWidget({
  chat_id: userId, // widgets work in private chats
  allow_queries: true,
  html: `<button id="b">Tap me</button>
<script>
  b.onclick = () => TelegramWidget.request("tap").then((a) => (b.textContent = a.result));
</script>`,
});

bot.on("widget_query", async (ctx) => {
  if (!("widget_query" in ctx.update)) return;
  const q = ctx.update.widget_query;
  await ctx.api.answerWidgetQuery({ widget_query_id: q.id, data: `hi ${ctx.from?.first_name}` });
});
```

#### Ephemeral Messages

- `chat_id` in the ephemeral-capable send methods and `receiver_user_id` in `EphemeralMessageParameters` are now optional, so `callback_query_id` alone sends an ephemeral reply to a callback query (in any chat except channel direct-messages chats).
- Types are stricter than the "Optional" columns in the Bot API docs, to catch at compile time what Telegram rejects at runtime:
  - A call to one of these methods without `chat_id` is a type error unless it is an ephemeral reply to a callback query (`callback_query_id` without `receiver_user_id`). The rule is the exported `ChatOrCallbackReply` type.
  - `EphemeralMessageParameters` must have `receiver_user_id` or `callback_query_id`. The callback-reply form is the exported `EphemeralCallbackReply` type.
  - `Omit` and `Pick` merge the members of these param types, so a wrapper such as `Omit<SendMessageParams, "parse_mode">` loses the rule and its spread is rejected. Use the exported `DistributiveOmit<SendMessageParams, "parse_mode">`. `Omit<SendMessageParams, "chat_id">` plus your own `chat_id` works as before. `interface X extends SendMessageParams` no longer compiles; use a `type` intersection.
- `ctx.reply` on an update without a chat (e.g. a callback query from an inline message) sends when `other` makes it an ephemeral reply to the callback query, instead of throwing.

```ts
bot.on("callback_query", async (ctx) => {
  const q = ctx.callbackQuery;
  if (!q) return;
  // No chat_id: shown only to the user who tapped, marked "Only visible to you"
  await ctx.api.sendMessage({
    text: "Only you can see this",
    ephemeral_message_parameters: { callback_query_id: q.id },
  });
  await ctx.answerCallbackQuery(); // still required after an ephemeral reply
});

await bot.api.sendMessage({ text: "hi" }); // ✗ type error: chat_id is required here

// Wrapping the param types: use DistributiveOmit, not Omit
import type { DistributiveOmit, SendMessageParams } from "node-telegram-bot-api";

const sendHtml = (p: DistributiveOmit<SendMessageParams, "parse_mode">) =>
  bot.api.sendMessage({ ...p, parse_mode: "HTML" });
```

#### Quotes from rich messages

- Added `rich_texts` to `TextQuote` and `quote_rich_texts` to `ReplyParameters`.

```ts
await bot.api.sendMessage({
  chat_id: chatId,
  text: "Agreed!",
  reply_parameters: {
    message_id: richMessageId,
    quote_rich_texts: ["the exact sentence being quoted"],
  },
});
```

#### TON wallet

- Added `TonWalletCard`, `TonWalletCardSticker`, `TonNft`, `TonNftAttribute`, and `ChatFullInfo.ton_wallet_card`.
- Added `TonWalletTransfer` and `Message.ton_wallet_transfer`.
- Renamed `StoryAreaPosition` to `AreaPosition`, following the Bot API. `StoryAreaPosition` stays as a deprecated alias.

